WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.751
To get a single subject
dance credential

2
00:00:01.751 --> 00:00:02.794
in California,

3
00:00:02.794 --> 00:00:05.672
Most people start by earning
a college degree in dance.

4
00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.881
This shows the state

5
00:00:06.881 --> 00:00:08.758
that you have subject matter competency,

6
00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:10.510
which I know you already do.

7
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.096
This is especially important
for the dance credential,

8
00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:14.597
because the programs
in the state

9
00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:17.350
teach you how to teach,
but not what to teach.

10
00:00:17.392 --> 00:00:18.560
That part comes from you.

11
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.978
If you don't have
a degree in dance,

12
00:00:19.978 --> 00:00:21.938
but you took at least 32 units

13
00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:24.357
of coursework in college, that is dance related,

14
00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.483
that will work too.

15
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.068
Once you have your bachelor's degree,

16
00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:29.446
you will apply to
and enroll in a program

17
00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:31.573
to get your single subject
credential in dance.

18
00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:33.450
And there are now more than 13 programs

19
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.161
all over the state from Sacramento to San Diego,

20
00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.537
where you can do just that.

21
00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.622
Some are totally remote
or online,

22
00:00:39.622 --> 00:00:40.957
some are fully in-person,

23
00:00:40.957 --> 00:00:42.667
and some have hybrid options.

24
00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.210
Take a look at the programs
and decide

25
00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.962
which one makes the most sense for you.

26
00:00:46.004 --> 00:00:48.256
Once you're in a single subject credential program,

27
00:00:48.256 --> 00:00:50.800
we'd also recommend getting a PE credential as well.

28
00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:52.802
That way, you'll be able to offer a dance class

29
00:00:52.802 --> 00:00:54.054
and your students can receive

30
00:00:54.095 --> 00:00:56.347
either dance or PE credits for the course.

31
00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.475
This makes you super marketable for schools,

32
00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:00.643
and learning
more is always a good thing.
